    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d521">

                <pb facs="0485" n="475" xml:id="pg475"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.94/1934: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The First Secretary of Embassy in China</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Smyth</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-01-27T15:00:00+08:00">January 27, 1941—3
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received January 27—7:18 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>42. Department’s 33 [<hi rendition="#italic">43</hi>], January 17, 8 p.m., to
                        Tokyo.<anchor n="28" xml:id="d521-f1"/> Marine-gendarme incident. Ambassador
                    Grew having informed this Embassy that he had an appointment with Foreign
                    Minister Matsuoka today, I called this morning on Counselor Tsuchida, in charge
                    of the Japanese Embassy here, and carried out the Department’s instructions. He
                    made no comments. Later, at lunch, I met Secretary Terasaki, who had been with
                    Mr. Tsuchida when I called. Mr. Terasaki said that he wished to assure me that
                    the official inquiry would be given the most serious consideration by the
                    Japanese Embassy.</p>
                <p>Sent to the Department. Repeated to Chungking, Tokyo, Shanghai.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Smyth</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
